# Nirva Shared Layer

`shared/` is imported by both client (`@shared/*`) and server (relative `../../shared/`).

## Core files

| File | Exports |
|------|---------|
| agents.ts | AGENTS[], Agent, AgentTier |
| agent-prompts.ts | AGENT_SYSTEM_PROMPTS |
| agent-details.ts | Extended agent profiles |
| organization.ts | AI_COMPANIES, CONTROL_TOWER, OrgAgentRole |
| model-orchestration.ts | MODEL_CATALOG, routeTask(), ORCHESTRATION_TIERS |
| ecosystem.ts | NIRVA_ECOSYSTEM, EcosystemApp |
| settings.ts | NirvaSettings, DEFAULT_SETTINGS, load/save |
| tenants.ts | Tenant types, default tenant |
| plugins.ts | Plugin definitions, categories |
| marketplace.ts | MarketplaceItem, categories |
| permissions.ts | Role permission matrix |
| const.ts | Shared constants |

## NirvaSettings (settings.ts)

```typescript
interface NirvaSettings {
  ollamaUrl: string;
  defaultModel: string;
  qdrantUrl: string;
  n8nUrl: string;
  useOrchestration: boolean;
  maxPremiumPercent: number;
  preferSelfHosted: boolean;
  ttsEnabled: boolean;
  ttsSpeed: number;
  wakeWord: string;
  notifyOnComplete: boolean;
  notifyOnError: boolean;
  obsidianUrl: string;
  obsidianApiKey: string;
  useObsidian: boolean;
}
```

Storage key: `nirva-settings` in localStorage.
Client loads via `loadClientSettings()` which merges env + stored + defaults.

## Model orchestration types

```typescript
type OrchestrationTier = "free" | "low_cost" | "premium";
interface ModelRouteDecision {
  agent: string;
  task: string;
  scores: TaskScores;
  recommendedTier: OrchestrationTier;
  model: ModelCatalogEntry;
  reasoning: string;
  reasoningTh: string;
}
```

Key exports: `routeTask()`, `routePipeline()`, `MODEL_CATALOG`, `ORCHESTRATION_RULES`

## Tenants (tenants.ts)

Multi-tenant isolation for tasks, plugins, marketplace.
Default tenant created on first run.

## Plugins (plugins.ts)

Plugin manifest format for agent extensions.
Categories: tool, data, integration, ui

## Marketplace (marketplace.ts)

Agent skill listings — export/import JSON format.
Rating, category, author, compatibility.

